Z||000000||Eric||04-18-2000||11:18 PM||||Just wondering if any of you guys with Gtechs ever turn them sideways to see what kind of lateral g's your car is capable of.  .94 g's is my best so far.  <P>88 GT with stock suspension<BR>205/60/15, 225/60/15 yokohama A509s  (treadwear rating 160, out of production)||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||04-19-2000||01:19 AM||||.94?!? That's great! I don't think GM even claimed that. (Did they?) All the production tolerances must have stacked up to your advantage.  ||||reg||14
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||04-19-2000||02:46 AM||||Wow! Let me tell you how much you have improved your grip if you don't know already!!! For the 88 GT Motortrend could only get a .84 for skid on stock tires in March of 88!<P>Congratulations on the improvement! Tires make the difference!<P>I have 225/50 16s on my 85 GT and I know someone who has aluminum bushings, eibach springs running Goodyear GS-C 225/50s in the front and 245s in the back on his 88 GT. Just think what he must be pulling!<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 04-19-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||Eric||04-19-2000||02:11 PM||||I really don't know how accurate that is.  I'm going to get a baseline from another car before I start patting myself on the back.  I should say, the suspension alignment has been altered from stock.  The rear tires have about -2degrees of camber.  And when I was doing the test, I tried repeatedly to throw the back end out so all four tires broke loose at once and the car wouldn't push.||||reg||1
Z||000004||loafer87gt||04-20-2000||02:50 PM||||Tires do make a BIG difference. I don't know why GM doesn't drop the Goodyear lineup as their OEM tires. They are really starting to hold back their vehicles. Look at the corvette in GT racing, it is running slower laps than anyone else, it is also the only car running goodyears, everyone else is running Firestones! Great work on the .94 G's. Way cool||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||04-20-2000||03:55 PM||||205-60-14 Yoko 509s! Konis, eibachs, sway bars and a drive better than I. pulled 1.12-3 in both directions. (right, left) the best i can do is about .9+ then I lose it the rear spills and i'm toast. (the better driver is, a teacher at Subaru/Panoz driving school and friend, and SCCA IT-B driver)  skill does make a difference! and MAN IS THAT COOL! to be in a car pulling those numbers! like having my nitrous on in a 200' circle!      What .g numbers can you guys pull on braking?  my best is 1.01  (x-drilled rears slotted fronts, Remsa pads, braided lines, new stock calipers) who can LOCK up their brakes! I've heard a bunch of you say your pedals are squishy and such...  I can lock up all 4! BlackGT was mad about that!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> he almost bought me a new back bumber! glad it's a 4 lane rd! ||||reg||1
Z||000006||lowCG||04-20-2000||05:57 PM||||Those Yoko 509s really rock,a similar tire,the Bridgstone(Firestone)RE71s are pretty much the same for incredible grip,good price.<BR>I don't like Goodyears either,after all they still sell the Eagle GT+4,a tire that I can remember from the early eighties.Might be good for that perfect restoration on an '81 Z-28,but otherwise they stink.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfiero||04-21-2000||05:21 PM||||My favorite tires of all time are the Bridgestone Potenza RE-71's too.  I just tried ordering a set for my '88 GT, but they have been discontinued by Bridgestone and are no longer available (at least that is what the Tire Rack told me).  <P>I did buy a set of Yokohama AVS Intermediates.....they also have a 160 treadwear (the RE-71's had a 180) AND they're cheap!  I paid $75 apiece for the fronts (205/60-15) and $81 apiece for the rear (215/60-15).<P>They're going on tomorrow (along with a good 4 wheel alignment).....I'll let everyone know what I think of them.<P>BTW.....I also have lowered springs, poly bushings and new KYB's, so this thing will stick to the road.  I wish I had one of those G-Tech things.....maybe I'll go buy one.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||10
Z||000008||1FST2M6||04-21-2000||08:09 PM||||I've got intermediates on my Alfa! (it's a 4 door) but it's an Alfa. (3liter V6 5spd. FWD 235hp @ the wheels from the factory!) Have Konis on it and Intrax Springs. I had Eagle HPs on it and they ARE CRAP!!! the AVSs STOMP NUTS! You'll LOVE them on your Fiero. I have a set of Yoko A032s  for my race tires (spare stocky 14s) for the fiero those are EXPONENTIALY better then the 509s! Make it a TOTALY different car! I'm sure you'll like the AVSs. how much camber are you planning on running? I have -1.25* in the rear and -.75* up front... tire may wear quicker but the handling is sharper.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Eric||04-21-2000||08:16 PM||||The yokos are great tires, they don't last long though.  I got about 8000 miles from the last set of rear tires (wore them bald Chadman can attest to that), but the fronts are only about half worn after 11,000.  You can drive so hard it's scary, they just don't break loose.  I can't wait for the autoX, I'm just gonna leave the Gtech on for the entire run and see what kind of numbers I can get.  I check out my breaking tommorow and post results (it's a little wet today).  <P>1FST2M6, have you ever tested the acceration g forces?  I tested mine today and got a consitant .35gs in second gear at 45 or so mph.  I couldn't look up in time to see what first registered.||||reg||1
Z||000010||mrfiero||04-22-2000||03:28 AM||||1FST2M6,<P>Thanks for the feedback on those Yokohamas and the Eagle HP's.  I too had a set of the HP's on a Formula and didn't really care for them.  It was a low mileage Formula so I didn't drive it hard, but still those tires broke loose way to easily.<P>It sounds like the Yokohamas will suit me just fine.  BTW....my GT is an auto., so I won't (can't?) spin the tires too much, so the rears should last a little longer than 8000 miles......I hope!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>As for the alignment.....it'll just be set to stock specs.  I have yet to find a shop in the Denver area that will set the alignment at anything other than what it is "supposed" to be.  <P>Thanks again.    ||||reg||10
Z||000011||1FST2M6||04-22-2000||08:18 PM||||1st gear under nitrous....   1.02!!! THAT LIFTS THE FRONT TIRES OFF THE GROUND! 2nd .73 3rd .31 and 4th only a LAME .27 at the shift...  with the nitrous off.. it blows... like a weak... .4 in 2nd...  I REALLY wish the nitrous power was ALWAYS there... oh well ... i'm working on it...   AN AUTOMATIC! I've been trying to trade my car for a white GT auto for MONTHS now... anyone?!?! ||||reg||1
